        836.0,
        802.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The $\\eta _ { \\mathrm { i n h } }$of the flexible polyimide film was 1.3 dL/g.",
      "evidence_id": "ev003"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_5_56",
      "page": 5,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        124.0,
        834.0,
        277.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Polyimides were synthesized from diamine BAPP and dianhydrides ODPA by a conventional two-step procedure: ring-opening polyaddition at room temperature to polyamic acid, followed by sequential heating of the polyamic acid films to $3 0 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$to obtain the corresponding polymers, as shown in Scheme 2.",
      "evidence_id": "ev004"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_5_56",
      "page": 5,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        124.0,
        834.0,
        277.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The bottom curve of Figure 1 gives the typical FTIR spectrum of polyimide.",
      "evidence_id": "ev005"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_5_57",
      "page": 5,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        277.0,
        833.0,
        414.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Thermograms of polyamic acid and polyimide are given in Figure 3.",
      "evidence_id": "ev006"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_5_58",
      "page": 5,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        415.0,
        834.0,
        554.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Figure 4 shows the DSC spectra of a typical poly(amic acid) and polyimide.",
      "evidence_id": "ev007"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_5_58",
      "page": 5,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        415.0,
        834.0,
        554.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The appearance of an endothermic peak in the range of $1 2 0 { - } 2 0 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$on the PAA curve is attributed not only to water produced in the process of cyclization, but also to the degradation of PAA occurring in this temperature region.",
      "evidence_id": "ev008"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_5_58",
      "page": 5,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        415.0,
        834.0,
        554.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "None of the polyimides exhibit a crystallization or melt transition in the DSC measurements.",
      "evidence_id": "ev009"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_5_58",
      "page": 5,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        415.0,
        834.0,
        554.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Therefore, the preparation of PI fibers has been carried out by spinning soluble polyimide dope in a phenol solvent instead of spinning PAA solution (17 – 19).",
      "evidence_id": "ev010"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_7_70",
      "page": 7,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        155.0,
        834.0,
        264.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Furthermore, the DSC thermogram of polyimide in Figure 4 shows a glass transition temperature $\\mathrm { ( T _ { g } ) }$of $2 3 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$.",
      "evidence_id": "ev011"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_7_70",
      "page": 7,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        155.0,
        834.0,
        264.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "This is a relatively lower value compared to those of common rigid polyimides and can probably be attributed to the flexibility of the polymer backbone containing –O– and ${ \\mathrm { > C } } ( \\mathrm { C H } _ { 3 } ) _ { 2 }$groups.",
      "evidence_id": "ev012"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_8_77",
      "page": 8,
      "bbox": [
        161.0,
        400.0,
        836.0,
        462.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Below $2 1 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$, the fact that $\\mathbf { E ^ { \\prime } }$is more than $\\mathrm { E } ^ { \\prime \\prime }$by one order of magnitude indicates that the polyimide exhibits an elastic behavior.",
      "evidence_id": "ev013"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_8_78",
      "page": 8,
      "bbox": [
        161.0,
        461.0,
        838.0,
        600.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The mechanical properties of polyamic acid and polyimide were measured under standard atmosphere.",
      "evidence_id": "ev014"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_8_78",
      "page": 8,
      "bbox": [
        161.0,
        461.0,
        838.0,
        600.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The elongation at break of PAA is only 6% and it does not exhibit an apparent yield.",
      "evidence_id": "ev015"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_8_78",
      "page": 8,
      "bbox": [
        161.0,
        461.0,
        838.0,
        600.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The measurement of mechanical properties indicates that the novel polyimide exhibits a yield behavior typical of thermoplastic polymers.",
      "evidence_id": "ev016"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "I_4_50",
      "page": 4,
      "bbox": [
        294.0,
        124.0,
        701.0,
        347.0
      ],
      "source_type": "image",
      "source_sentence": "Figure 1. FTIR spectra of BNPP, BAPP, and polyimide (PI).",
      "evidence_id": "ev017"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_3_41",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        124.0,
        834.0,
        233.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "To measure the mechanical properties, the polymer films were cut into strips with a width of ${ \\sim } 5 $mm in advance.",
      "evidence_id": "ev018"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_2_35",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        161.0,
        710.0,
        836.0,
        802.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The film was cast onto a glass plate, followed by heating this solution of polyamic acid for 2 h at $8 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$1 h at $1 2 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ,$1 h at $1 8 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ,$1 h at $2 5 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$1 h to $3 0 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$.",
      "evidence_id": "ev019"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_2_35",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        161.0,
        710.0,
        836.0,
        802.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "ODPA was added to the solution of BAPP in DMAc in several portions. The mixture was stirred at $0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$for 20 h under an atmosphere of $\\Nu _ { 2 }$to form the polyamic acid. The film was cast onto a glass plate, followed by heating this solution of polyamic acid for 2 h at $8 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$1 h at $1 2 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ,$1 h at $1 8 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ,$1 h at $2 5 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$1 h to $3 0 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$. The $\\eta _ { \\mathrm { i n h } }$of the flexible polyimide film was 1.3 dL/g. DMAc was partly evaporated at $1 2 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$and completely evaporated at $1 8 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$, since the boiling point of the solvent is ${ \\sim } 1 6 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$",
      "evidence_id": "ev020"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_3_41",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        124.0,
        834.0,
        233.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The DSC analysis was performed on a TA Instruments DSC $8 2 2 ^ { \\mathrm { e } }$in flowing nitrogen at a heating rate of $1 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } / \\mathrm { m i n }$. Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) was performed on a Perkin-Elmer TGA 7 analyzer and the thermal stability of samples was determined in $\\Nu _ { 2 }$at a heating rate of $1 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } / \\mathrm { m i n } .$. To measure the mechanical properties, the polymer films were cut into strips with a width of ${ \\sim } 5 $mm in advance. The measurement was conducted on an XQ-1 instrument with a gauge length of 20 mm and a crosshead speed of 5 mm/min. Each specimen was measured five times and the values were averaged.",
      "evidence_id": "ev021"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_3_41",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        124.0,
        834.0,
        233.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The DSC analysis was performed on a TA Instruments DSC $8 2 2 ^ { \\mathrm { e } }$ in flowing nitrogen at a heating rate of $1 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } / \\mathrm { m i n }$.",
      "evidence_id": "ev022"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_3_41",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        124.0,
        834.0,
        233.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) was performed on a Perkin-Elmer TGA 7 analyzer and the thermal stability of samples was determined in $\\Nu _ { 2 }$ at a heating rate of $1 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } / \\mathrm { m i n } .$.",
      "evidence_id": "ev023"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_3_41",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        124.0,
        834.0,
        233.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "To measure the mechanical properties, the polymer films were cut into strips with a width of ${ \\sim } 5 $mm in advance. The measurement was conducted on an XQ-1 instrument with a gauge length of 20 mm and a crosshead speed of 5 mm/min. Each specimen was measured five times and the values were averaged.",
      "evidence_id": "ev025"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_7_70",
      "page": 7,
      "bbox": [
        157.0,
        155.0,
        834.0,
        264.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The DMA spectra of polyimide in Figure 5b show a loss tangent (tan d) peak at $2 2 5 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$, which means $\\mathrm { T _ { g } }$ at this temperature.",
      "evidence_id": "ev026"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_2_35",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        161.0,
        710.0,
        836.0,
        802.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The $\\eta _ { \\mathrm { i n h } }$ of the flexible polyimide film was 1.3 dL/g.",
      "evidence_id": "ev027"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_8_78",
      "page": 8,
      "bbox": [
        161.0,
        461.0,
        838.0,
        600.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The maximum elongation at break is 29%.",
      "evidence_id": "ev028"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_8_78",
      "page": 8,
      "bbox": [
        161.0,
        461.0,
        838.0,
        600.0
      ],
      "source_type": "text",
      "source_sentence": "The obvious yield behavior at an elongation of ~14% is shown in the S–S curves of polyimide.",
      "evidence_id": "ev029"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "P_8_78",
